{"name":"Memory Lane","hex":"#c7d1db","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Memory Lane","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of memory lane."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Memory_Lane"}],"entries":[{"title":"Memory Lane (2024 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Memory Lane is a 2024 comedy-drama film written by Marijn de Wit and co-written and directed by Jelle de Jonge. The film was a big box office hit in The Netherlands and was awarded the Golden Film. It was chosen as the Dutch entry for the Best International Feature Film at the 97th Academy Awards. The film won two Golden Calf awards for best feature film and best leading role for Leny Breederveld. The winners were announced at the Netherlands Film Festival."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b6/Memory_Lane_%282024_film%29_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_Lane_(2024_film)","wikidata":"Q130316199"},{"title":"Memory Lane (2012 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Memory Lane is a 2012 science-fiction film by American director Shawn Holmes and his directorial debut. The film world-premiered on May 6, 2012, at the Sci-Fi-London film festival in London, England and was funded by Shawn Holmes with a budget of less than $300."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Memory_Lane_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_Lane_(2012_film)","wikidata":"Q19864804"},{"title":"Memory Lane (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Memory Lane is the fifth studio album by American country music band Old Dominion. It was released on October 6, 2023, via Sony Music Nashville's RCA Nashville imprint. It was preceded by the release of its title track and \"Can't Break Up Now\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/MemoryLaneOldDominion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_Lane_(album)","wikidata":"Q123125324"},{"title":"Memory","blocks":[{"text":"Memory is the faculty of the mind by which data or information is encoded, stored, and retrieved when needed. It is the retention of information over time for the purpose of influencing future action. If past events could not be remembered, it would be impossible for language, relationships, or personal identity to develop. Memory loss is usually described as forgetfulness or a disorder such as amnesia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Memory.gif/330px-Memory.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory","wikidata":"Q492"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg/500px-Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg/1280px-Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg/500px-Memory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Olin Levi Warner's 1896 illustration, Memory, now housed in the Thomas Jefferson Building at the Library of Congress in Washington, D.C.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMemory-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Multistore_model.png/250px-Multistore_model.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bf/Multistore_model.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten